is like putting the period

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:53.370
at the end of a sentence.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:54.240
When you make a photograph,

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:56.310
all of the work happens beforehand.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:58.380
That's just like it is with you.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:11:59.460
- [Melissa] Yeah, I guess with cooking,

00:11:59.460 --> 00:12:01.740
the journey that dish has gone through,

00:12:01.740 --> 00:12:04.680
it all ends at the moment
the person actually tastes,

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:07.650
and the flavors and the memories
that are attached to it.

00:12:07.650 --> 00:12:08.769
- [Kiliii] That's really cool.

00:12:08.769 --> 00:12:09.663
It's kind of amazing how similar that is.

00:12:09.663 --> 00:12:11.610
- It's very similar.

00:12:11.610 --> 00:12:13.554
All right, let's check out this fish.

00:12:13.554 --> 00:12:14.910
- Oh cool, the big reveal.

00:12:14.910 --> 00:12:16.233
- Oh, it smells good.

00:12:18.420 --> 00:12:20.023
Check it out.

00:12:20.023 --> 00:12:21.843
- Cool.
- That looks awesome.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:24.900
- Whoa, nice.

00:12:24.900 --> 00:12:26.400
- Slow cooked right there.

00:12:26.400 --> 00:12:28.440
That's a big filet for you.

00:12:28.440 --> 00:12:29.493
- [Kiliii] Woohoo.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:32.223
- Oh, that's looking perfect.

00:12:33.090 --> 00:12:33.923
- [Kiliii] Brilliant.

00:12:33.923 --> 00:12:34.756
- Okay.

00:12:35.610 --> 00:12:38.430
Some of this salsa verde on there.

00:12:38.430 --> 00:12:40.530
- [Kiliii] Awesome, what a cool pairing.

00:12:40.530 --> 00:12:42.450
- That's yours right there, my friend.

00:12:42.450 --> 00:12:43.320
- [Kiliii] Beautimous, thank you.

00:12:43.320 --> 00:12:45.210
- All right, should we sit down and eat?

00:12:45.210 --> 00:12:46.043
- Yeah.

00:12:49.500 --> 00:12:51.240
Such a familiar and lovely smell.

00:12:51.240 --> 00:12:52.200
Oh yeah.
- Cheers.

00:12:52.200 --> 00:12:53.200
- All right, cheers.

00:12:56.340 --> 00:12:58.503
- Yeah, yeah, very good.

00:12:59.400 --> 00:13:00.783
- I'm excited about this.

00:13:03.300 --> 00:13:05.190
- Mm, no, that's excellent.

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:06.150
Compliments to the chef!

00:13:06.150 --> 00:13:08.400
Well done, well done!

00:13:08.400 --> 00:13:09.240
Yeah.

00:13:09.240 --> 00:13:11.430
I can definitely taste
the natural world in this.

00:13:11.430 --> 00:13:12.570
It's excellent.

00:13:12.570 --> 00:13:13.800
- Thank you.

00:13:13.800 --> 00:13:16.230
I've salt baked many fish in my career,

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:17.490
but never like this,

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:20.760
and so thank you for just
showing me the outdoors,

00:13:20.760 --> 00:13:22.590
taking me to new places,

00:13:22.590 --> 00:13:24.330
and helping me find inspiration

00:13:24.330 --> 00:13:26.460
in ways that I never thought.

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.140
- No, thank you. (laughing)

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:29.580
Really, thank you.

00:13:29.580 --> 00:13:31.230
- The only thing that's
gonna make this better

00:13:31.230 --> 00:13:32.930
is if we catch the fish next time.

00:13:34.110 --> 00:13:34.943
- All right.

00:13:34.943 --> 00:13:36.210
Next time, singing for trout.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:37.411
- You're taking me out.

00:13:37.411 --> 00:13:38.244
- Okay.

00:13:38.244 --> 00:13:39.911
- Geonbae.
- Geonbae!

00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:45.210
Maybe it's the mountain
air, or the glacial waters,

00:13:45.210 --> 00:13:48.540
